<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Configuration for HabitLockAccessibilityService.

  canRetrieveWindowContent is TRUE, and that is a deliberate, costly choice.

  It was false until surface blocking existed, because the package name of the
  foreground app arrives on the event itself and nothing more was needed. Blocking a
  single surface - the Reels tab but not a reel a friend sent you - cannot be done from
  the package name alone: both are com.instagram.android. Telling them apart requires
  reading the view hierarchy.

  What this app actually does with that access is narrow and enforced in one auditable
  file, ViewIdCollector.kt: it reads getViewIdResourceName() and NOTHING else. Node
  text, content descriptions and hint text are never read, nothing is stored beyond the
  event being handled, and the manifest requests no network permission, so nothing can
  leave the device.

  typeWindowContentChanged is added alongside typeWindowStateChanged because moving
  between tabs inside Instagram does not always produce a state change - without it,
  opening Reels from the home feed would go unnoticed.

  flagReportViewIds is REQUIRED and its absence was a real shipped bug. Without it
  Android returns null from getViewIdResourceName() for every node, even with
  canRetrieveWindowContent granted - so the tree could be walked but every id came back
  empty and no surface rule could ever match. The user's diagnostics report showed
  exactly this: a verdict recorded for each app, and not a single view id under any of
  them. canRetrieveWindowContent buys the tree; this flag buys the ids in it.

  There is still no android:isAccessibilityTool. This is a self-control tool, not an
  accessibility aid, and falsely declaring otherwise trips Play Protect's "Deceptive
  Accessibility Tool" warning.
-->
<accessibility-service xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:accessibilityEventTypes="typeWindowStateChanged|typeWindowContentChanged"
    android:accessibilityFeedbackType="feedbackGeneric"
    android:accessibilityFlags="flagReportViewIds|flagRetrieveInteractiveWindows"
    android:notificationTimeout="200"
    android:canRetrieveWindowContent="true"
    android:description="@string/accessibility_service_description" />
